@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Evaluator
+
+From `code_map/`:
+
+```sh
+bun eval/run.ts --tool "bun eval/stub/stub.ts" --cases eval/cases/fixtures.json --out /tmp/cm-eval
+```
+
+From the repository root, the bundled case paths work unchanged:
+
+```sh
+bun code_map/eval/run.ts --tool "bun code_map/eval/stub/stub.ts" --out /tmp/cm-eval
+```
+
+Additional `--cases` files follow the spec's format. The shell tool command is trusted; appended case arguments are shell quoted. Paths in external case files are relative to the invoking working directory. The evaluator reads JSON stdout and preserves the full command, exit status, stdout, stderr, changed-file list and expectation mismatches in `report.json`. `report.md` presents the requirement/line statuses and failures. Runs are sequential so snapshots belong to one invocation.
+
+The 34 fixture cases exercise the 18 fixture-checkable Fails-if lines, with runtime marker checks and R3 observations on every invocation. A6 and L2 are NOT CHECKED without the external evaluation work. The report also states the agent/privacy parts it cannot establish. See [SPEC_QUESTIONS.md](SPEC_QUESTIONS.md).
+
+`stub/answers/<case-id>.json` contains each editable canned answer. Change a location, resolution, count, limit, or fake label and rerun: the evaluator should report NOT MET. Identical commands have identical canned files; the stub rejects disagreement among them, so changing any one is observable. Unknown commands print the empty static-analysis answer required by the brief.
+
+These checks were written by P2 Codex independently of the future builder. Passing the stub validates evaluator plumbing and its known answers. It does not establish correctness of a future tool on other source projects.
diff --git a/code_map/eval/SPEC_QUESTIONS.md b/code_map/eval/SPEC_QUESTIONS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d596680343c0e10ae2125ece2a261c721798ab07
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/SPEC_QUESTIONS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Spec questions and evaluator scope
+
+Author: P2 Codex. These are implementation readings, not changes to the requirements or spec.
+
+| Question | Narrow reading used |
+|---|---|
+| What makes a relative case-file path relative? | External case `root` and `project` paths are relative to the evaluator's working directory, following the example's `root: "."`. The bundled fixture case file uses package-relative paths so the two invocation forms in the brief both work. `--cases` itself is relative to the working directory. |
+| How does `equals` work with `[]` or recursive `children`? | A simple path compares its single selected value. A path using `[]` or `children` compares the complete selected list, in traversal order. An absent simple path is missing, not JSON `null`; an empty wildcard selection is `[]`. `children` visits descendants in source/depth-first order, never the current step. |
+| What happens for `tests --file` without `--per-function`? | The tool may give an empty JSON answer with an explanatory limit; it must not return a per-function report. The fixture does not prescribe the explanation's wording. The spec defines no positive per-function JSON shape, so the evaluator does not invent one. |
+| What are evaluator exit codes? | 0 means a report completed without NOT MET cases; NOT CHECKED is allowed. 1 means NOT MET cases. 2 means invalid evaluator input or an evaluator/environment failure. |
+| Where is the R1 marker path for external cases? | The case format has no marker field. Runtime marker checks use only the known bundled `marker/EXECUTED.marker`, after every invocation (including the four required commands). An external R1 case alone is NOT CHECKED for the runtime part. The evaluator removes only its own marker. |
+| Does `unshare -rn` detect connection attempts? | It isolates network access; it does not trace syscalls. Nonzero tool exit and filesystem changes fail the bounded check. A connection failure caught inside a successful tool cannot be detected from stdout. Such attempts and the broader privacy/training promise remain explicitly NOT CHECKED in `uncheckedParts`. No syscall tracer dependency is introduced. |
+| Does isolation establish all of R3? | No. R3's MET line describes the spec-assigned isolation and before/after filesystem observation only. Snapshots hash regular files and retain mode, timestamps and symlink targets under `--root` and cwd; links are not followed. Files outside those trees, transient changes restored between snapshots, and transmissions by other processes are not observed. A missing/denied `unshare` makes R3 NOT CHECKED, even if snapshots are unchanged. |
+| How are combined tool/agent Fails-if lines reported? | Line statuses describe the evaluator's tool checks. `uncheckedParts` separately records A2 candidate choice/naming, A3 asking the user, and A5 whether the user asked. These belong to P6; a MET tool line does not assert that the agent part passed. |
+| Can a fixture check A6 or L2? | No. No A6 claim is made without external cases for the three real opencode modules. L2 is P5's independent comparison. Both remain NOT CHECKED in the bundled suite. |
+| How does an external case certify A6? | The spec supplies no module-certification field or A1 linkage field. An A6 case is therefore NOT CHECKED unless the three module-map commands and A1 case checks on those same commands are present; module location is identified by the three specified path suffixes. |
+
+Requirements check: **who decides**, **one thing**, **unit**, **can it fail**, **weak words**, **level**, **basis**, and **links** pass for the concrete evaluator contract when read as the author's accepted spec and fixture checks. The unresolved interface details above affect **who decides** or **can it fail**; the brief explicitly assigns their recording and the narrowest reading to this evaluator. No numeric threshold, acceptance criterion, or new dependency is added.
diff --git a/code_map/eval/case-file.ts b/code_map/eval/case-file.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..405543c2ccf065ae61f3b1641dec03908f5f2fea
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/case-file.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+import { readFile } from "node:fs/promises";
+import { resolve } from "node:path";
+import { isObject, selectPath, type Expectation } from "./matcher.ts";
+import { requirementLines, type Requirement } from "./requirements.ts";
+
+export type EvalCase = { id: string; requirement: Requirement; line: string; args: string[]; expect: Expectation };
+export type CaseFile = { project: string[]; root: string; tests: string[]; cases: EvalCase[] };
+export type LoadedCaseFile = CaseFile & { source: string };
+
+function stringArray(value: unknown): value is string[] {
+  return Array.isArray(value) && value.every(item => typeof item === "string");
+}
+
+export function validateCaseFile(value: unknown): CaseFile {
+  if (!isObject(value) || !stringArray(value.project) || !value.project.length ||
+      typeof value.root !== "string" || !stringArray(value.tests) || !Array.isArray(value.cases)) {
+    throw new Error("Case file needs project: string[], root: string, tests: string[], cases: array");
+  }
+  const ids = new Set<string>();
+  for (const candidate of value.cases) {
+    if (!isObject(candidate) || typeof candidate.id !== "string" || !candidate.id || ids.has(candidate.id) ||
+        typeof candidate.requirement !== "string" || !(candidate.requirement in requirementLines) ||
+        typeof candidate.line !== "string" || !stringArray(candidate.args) || !candidate.args.length || !isObject(candidate.expect)) {
+      throw new Error("Invalid or duplicate case: " + JSON.stringify(candidate));
+    }
+    ids.add(candidate.id);
+    const lines: readonly string[] = requirementLines[candidate.requirement as Requirement];
+    if (!lines.includes(candidate.line.replace(/\.$/, ""))) throw new Error(`Unknown Fails-if line in ${candidate.id}: ${candidate.line}`);
+    candidate.line = candidate.line.replace(/\.$/, "");
+    const expect = candidate.expect;
+    if (!Array.isArray(expect.includes) || !Array.isArray(expect.excludes) || !Array.isArray(expect.equals) ||
+        ![true, false, null].includes(expect.ambiguous as boolean | null) || !stringArray(expect.limitReasons)) {
+      throw new Error(`Invalid expectation in ${candidate.id}`);
+    }
+    for (const location of [...expect.includes, ...expect.excludes]) {
+      if (!isObject(location) || typeof location.path !== "string" || typeof location.file !== "string" ||
+          !Number.isInteger(location.line) || (location.line as number) < 1) throw new Error(`Invalid location in ${candidate.id}`);
+      selectPath({}, location.path);
+    }
+    for (const equality of expect.equals) {
+      if (!isObject(equality) || typeof equality.path !== "string" || !Object.hasOwn(equality, "value")) {
+        throw new Error(`Invalid equality in ${candidate.id}`);
+      }
+      selectPath({}, equality.path);
+    }
+  }
+  return value as CaseFile;
+}
+
+export async function loadCaseFile(path: string): Promise<LoadedCaseFile> {
+  const source = resolve(path);
+  const value = validateCaseFile(JSON.parse(await readFile(source, "utf8")));
+  // Bundled examples remain runnable from either the repository or the package directory.
+  const base = source === resolve(import.meta.dir, "cases/fixtures.json") ? resolve(import.meta.dir, "..") : process.cwd();
+  return { ...value, source, root: resolve(base, value.root), project: value.project.map(project => resolve(base, project)) };
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/contract.ts b/code_map/eval/contract.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cdc73c588b836def841737343bd78ee33281b0c4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/contract.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,181 @@
+import { isObject, type Mismatch } from "./matcher.ts";
+
+const nodeKinds = ["function", "method", "arrow", "effect-fn", "property", "class", "variable", "interface-member", "other"];
+const limitKinds = ["depth", "dynamic", "outside-repo", "other-process", "not-found", "seen", "other"];
+const stepKinds = ["call", "if", "else", "loop", "try", "catch", "return", "yield*"];
+
+export function validateAnswer(answer: unknown, args: string[], testPatterns: string[]): Mismatch[] {
+  const failures: Mismatch[] = [];
+  const fail = (path: string, expected: unknown, actual: unknown) => failures.push({ path, expected,
+    actual: actual === undefined ? { missing: true } : actual, message: "JSON contract violated" });
+  function location(value: unknown, path: string): value is Record<string, unknown> {
+    if (!isObject(value) || typeof value.file !== "string" || !value.file || value.file.startsWith("/") ||
+        !Number.isInteger(value.line) || (value.line as number) < 1 ||
+        (value.endLine !== undefined && (!Number.isInteger(value.endLine) || (value.endLine as number) < (value.line as number)))) {
+      fail(path, "relative file and positive 1-based line (endLine >= line)", value); return false;
+    }
+    return true;
+  }
+  function node(value: unknown, path: string): value is Record<string, unknown> {
+    if (!location(value, path)) return false;
+    if (typeof value.name !== "string" || !value.name || !nodeKinds.includes(value.kind as string)) {
+      fail(path, "named Node with a spec kind", value); return false;
+    }
+    return true;
+  }
+  function limit(value: unknown, path: string) {
+    if (!isObject(value) || !limitKinds.includes(value.reason as string)) { fail(path, "Limit with stated reason", value); return; }
+    if (value.at !== undefined) location(value.at, path + ".at");
+    if (value.ref !== undefined) location(value.ref, path + ".ref");
+    if (value.reason === "seen" && value.ref === undefined) fail(path, "seen limit with ref", value);
+    if (value.reason === "other" && (typeof value.text !== "string" || !value.text.trim())) fail(path, "other limit with text", value);
+  }
+  function array(value: unknown, path: string, visit: (item: unknown, path: string) => void) {
+    if (!Array.isArray(value)) { fail(path, "array", value); return; }
+    value.forEach((item, index) => visit(item, `${path}[${index}]`));
+  }
+  function link(value: unknown, path: string) {
+    if (!isObject(value)) { fail(path, "Link", value); return; }
+    node(value.from, path + ".from"); location(value.site, path + ".site");
+    if (!["call", "new", "service-call"].includes(value.kind as string)) fail(path + ".kind", "call | new | service-call", value.kind);
+    if (!["definition", "implementation-lookup"].includes(value.via as string)) fail(path + ".via", "definition | implementation-lookup", value.via);
+    if (value.declaration !== undefined) location(value.declaration, path + ".declaration");
+    array(value.candidates, path + ".candidates", (candidate, at) => {
+      if (!node(candidate, at)) return;
+      const testFake = testPatterns.some(pattern => new Bun.Glob(pattern).match(candidate.file as string));
+      if (candidate.testFake !== testFake) fail(at + ".testFake", testFake, candidate.testFake);
+    });
+    const real = Array.isArray(value.candidates) ? value.candidates.filter(candidate => isObject(candidate) && candidate.testFake === false) : [];
+    const expectedResolution = real.length === 0 ? "unresolved" : real.length === 1 ? "implementation" : "ambiguous";
+    if (value.resolution !== expectedResolution) fail(path + ".resolution", expectedResolution, value.resolution);
+    if (value.resolution === "implementation") {
+      if (node(value.to, path + ".to")) {
+        const target = value.to;
+        if (!real.some(candidate => candidate.file === target.file && candidate.line === target.line)) {
+          fail(path + ".to", "the sole non-test candidate", value.to);
+        }
+        if (value.to.kind === "interface-member" || (value.via === "implementation-lookup" && isObject(value.declaration) &&
+            value.to.file === value.declaration.file && value.to.line === value.declaration.line)) {
+          fail(path + ".to", "an implementation, rather than its interface declaration", value.to);
+        }
+      }
+    } else if (value.to !== undefined) fail(path + ".to", "absent for unresolved or ambiguous links", value.to);
+    if (value.resolution === "unresolved" && (typeof value.reason !== "string" || !value.reason.trim())) fail(path + ".reason", "unresolved reason", value.reason);
+  }
+  function flowStep(value: unknown, path: string) {
+    if (!isObject(value)) { fail(path, "Step", value); return; }
+    location(value.at, path + ".at");
+    if (!stepKinds.includes(value.kind as string)) fail(path + ".kind", stepKinds, value.kind);
+    if (typeof value.text !== "string" || !value.text.trim()) fail(path + ".text", "full source text", value.text);
+    if (value.children !== undefined) array(value.children, path + ".children", flowStep);
+  }
+  if (!isObject(answer)) { fail("$", "Answer object", answer); return failures; }
+  const fields = ["command", "query", "ambiguous", "matches", "links", "chain", "tests", "map", "limits", "empty"];
+  for (const key of Object.keys(answer)) if (!fields.includes(key)) fail(key, "specified Answer fields only", answer[key]);
+  if (answer.command !== args[0]) fail("command", args[0], answer.command);
+  array(answer.limits, "limits", limit);
+  if (answer.query !== undefined && (!Array.isArray(answer.query) || !answer.query.every(query => typeof query === "string"))) fail("query", "string[]", answer.query);
+  if (answer.empty !== undefined && answer.empty !== "none found by static analysis") fail("empty", "none found by static analysis", answer.empty);
+  if (args[0] !== "map" && answer.map !== undefined) fail("map", "absent for a specific question", answer.map);
+  if (answer.matches !== undefined) {
+    array(answer.matches, "matches", node);
+    if (Array.isArray(answer.matches) && answer.ambiguous !== (answer.matches.length > 1)) fail("ambiguous", answer.matches.length > 1, answer.ambiguous);
+    if (answer.ambiguous === true && args[0] !== "find" && args[0] !== "where" &&
+        [answer.links, answer.chain, answer.tests, answer.map].some(value => value !== undefined)) fail("$", "ambiguous name: candidates only", answer);
+  }
+  if (answer.links !== undefined) array(answer.links, "links", link);
+  if (answer.chain !== undefined) {
+    if (!isObject(answer.chain)) fail("chain", "{up, down}", answer.chain);
+    else for (const direction of ["up", "down"] as const) {
+      const depthFlag = args.indexOf("--" + direction);
+      const depth = depthFlag < 0 ? 6 : Number(args[depthFlag + 1]);
+      const expanded = new Set<string>();
+      const rootMatch = /^(.*):(\d+)$/.exec(args[1] ?? "");
+      if (rootMatch) expanded.add(`${rootMatch[1]}:${rootMatch[2]}`);
+      function chainStep(value: unknown, path: string, level: number) {
+        if (!isObject(value)) { fail(path, "ChainStep", value); return; }
+        if (value.level !== level || level > depth) fail(path + ".level", `level ${level}, at most ${depth}`, value.level);
+        link(value.link, path + ".link");
+        if (value.stop !== undefined) limit(value.stop, path + ".stop");
+        const target = isObject(value.link) ? value.link[direction === "down" ? "to" : "from"] : undefined;
+        if (isObject(target)) {
+          const key = `${target.file}:${target.line}`;
+          if (expanded.has(key)) {
+            if (!isObject(value.stop) || value.stop.reason !== "seen" || !isObject(value.stop.ref) ||
+                value.stop.ref.file !== target.file || value.stop.ref.line !== target.line) fail(path + ".stop", "seen with reference to first occurrence", value.stop);
+          } else {
+            if (isObject(value.stop) && value.stop.reason === "seen") fail(path + ".stop", "reference to an already shown function", value.stop);
+            expanded.add(key);
+          }
+        }
+        if (Array.isArray(value.children) && value.children.length && value.stop !== undefined) fail(path + ".children", "no expansion after a stop", value.children);
+        if (level === depth && value.stop === undefined) fail(path + ".stop", "depth stop", value.stop);
+        array(value.children, path + ".children", (child, at) => chainStep(child, at, level + 1));
+      }
+      array(answer.chain[direction], `chain.${direction}`, (step, at) => chainStep(step, at, 1));
+    }
+  }
+  if (answer.tests !== undefined) {
+    if (args.includes("--file") && !args.includes("--per-function")) fail("tests", "absent without --per-function", answer.tests);
+    if (!isObject(answer.tests)) fail("tests", "TestsAnswer", answer.tests);
+    else {
+      if (answer.tests.label !== "static-call-path") fail("tests.label", "static-call-path", answer.tests.label);
+      if (!Array.isArray(answer.tests.tests) || answer.tests.count !== answer.tests.tests.length) fail("tests.count", Array.isArray(answer.tests.tests) ? answer.tests.tests.length : "tests.length", answer.tests.count);
+      const testCase = (value: unknown, path: string) => {
+        if (!location(value, path)) return;
+        if (typeof value.name !== "string" || !value.name.trim()) fail(path + ".name", "test case name", value.name);
+        if (!Array.isArray(value.path) || !value.path.length) fail(path + ".path", "nonempty evidence path", value.path);
+        array(value.path, path + ".path", link);
+        const throughFake = Array.isArray(value.path) && value.path.some(edge => isObject(edge) && edge.kind === "service-call" &&
+          Array.isArray(edge.candidates) && edge.candidates.some(candidate => isObject(candidate) && candidate.testFake === true));
+        if (value.throughFake !== throughFake) fail(path + ".throughFake", throughFake, value.throughFake);
+        if (Array.isArray(value.path)) for (let index = 1; index < value.path.length; index++) {
+          const previous = value.path[index - 1]; const next = value.path[index];
+          if (isObject(previous) && isObject(previous.to) && isObject(next) && isObject(next.from) &&
+              (previous.to.file !== next.from.file || previous.to.line !== next.from.line)) fail(path + ".path", "connected static call path", value.path);
+        }
+      };
+      array(answer.tests.tests, "tests.tests", testCase);
+      array(answer.tests.undecided, "tests.undecided", testCase);
+      const fakeFlag = args.indexOf("--fake-rule"); const rule = fakeFlag < 0 ? undefined : args[fakeFlag + 1];
+      const countedFakes = Array.isArray(answer.tests.tests) && answer.tests.tests.some(test => isObject(test) && test.throughFake === true);
+      if (rule !== "count" && countedFakes) fail("tests.tests", "fakes counted only with --fake-rule count", answer.tests.tests);
+      if (rule !== undefined && Array.isArray(answer.tests.undecided) && answer.tests.undecided.length) fail("tests.undecided", [], answer.tests.undecided);
+      if (rule === undefined && Array.isArray(answer.tests.undecided) && answer.tests.undecided.length &&
+          (!Array.isArray(answer.limits) || !answer.limits.some(limit => isObject(limit) && limit.reason === "other" && limit.text === "fake rule not set (A3)"))) fail("limits", "fake rule not set (A3)", answer.limits);
+    }
+  }
+  if (answer.map !== undefined) {
+    if (!isObject(answer.map)) fail("map", "ModuleMap", answer.map);
+    else {
+      array(answer.map.definitions, "map.definitions", node); array(answer.map.links, "map.links", link);
+      array(answer.map.entries, "map.entries", (entry, path) => {
+        if (!isObject(entry)) { fail(path, "entry", entry); return; }
+        node(entry.fn, path + ".fn"); array(entry.steps, path + ".steps", flowStep);
+      });
+      if (answer.map.siblings !== undefined) {
+        if (!isObject(answer.map.siblings)) fail("map.siblings", "siblings table", answer.map.siblings);
+        else {
+          array(answer.map.siblings.members, "map.siblings.members", (member, path) => {
+            if (typeof member !== "string") fail(path, "member file", member);
+          });
+          array(answer.map.siblings.rows, "map.siblings.rows", (row, path) => {
+            if (!isObject(row)) { fail(path, "sibling concern", row); return; }
+            if (typeof row.concern !== "string" || !row.concern || !["shared", "varies", "unclear"].includes(row.status as string)) fail(path, "named shared/varies/unclear concern", row);
+            array(row.cells, path + ".cells", (cell, at) => {
+              if (!isObject(cell) || typeof cell.member !== "string" || typeof cell.text !== "string" || !cell.text.trim()) fail(at, "member, text and at", cell);
+              else location(cell.at, at + ".at");
+            });
+          });
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  }
+  const collections = [answer.matches, answer.links];
+  if (isObject(answer.chain)) collections.push(answer.chain.up, answer.chain.down);
+  if (isObject(answer.tests)) collections.push(answer.tests.tests, answer.tests.undecided);
+  if (isObject(answer.map)) collections.push(answer.map.definitions, answer.map.links, answer.map.entries);
+  const empty = collections.every(value => value === undefined || (Array.isArray(value) && value.length === 0));
+  if (empty !== (answer.empty !== undefined)) fail("empty", empty ? "none found by static analysis" : "absent for a nonempty answer", answer.empty);
+  return failures;
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/matcher.ts b/code_map/eval/matcher.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c7fa853a59902a5c54d19be935b1de992f2134dd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/matcher.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+import { isDeepStrictEqual } from "node:util";
+
+export type LocationExpectation = { path: string; file: string; line: number };
+export type Expectation = {
+  includes: LocationExpectation[];
+  excludes: LocationExpectation[];
+  equals: { path: string; value: unknown }[];
+  ambiguous: boolean | null;
+  limitReasons: string[];
+};
+export type Mismatch = { path: string; expected: unknown; actual: unknown; message: string };
+
+export function isObject(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {
+  return value !== null && typeof value === "object" && !Array.isArray(value);
+}
+
+function descendants(value: unknown): unknown[] {
+  if (!isObject(value) || !Array.isArray(value.children)) return [];
+  return value.children.flatMap(child => [child, ...descendants(child)]);
+}
+
+/** Missing values stay absent; [] collects values, and children searches descendants. */
+export function selectPath(value: unknown, path: string): unknown[] {
+  let values: unknown[] = [value];
+  for (const segment of path.split(".")) {
+    const match = /^([A-Za-z_$][\w$]*)(\[\])?$/.exec(segment);
+    if (!match) throw new Error(`Invalid expectation path: ${path}`);
+    const key = match[1]!;
+    const array = Boolean(match[2]);
+    values = values.flatMap(parent => {
+      if (key === "children") return descendants(parent);
+      if (!isObject(parent) || !Object.hasOwn(parent, key)) return [];
+      const child = parent[key];
+      return array ? (Array.isArray(child) ? child : []) : [child];
+    });
+  }
+  return values;
+}
+
+export function collectLimitReasons(value: unknown): string[] {
+  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value.flatMap(collectLimitReasons);
+  if (!isObject(value)) return [];
+  const reasons: string[] = [];
+  if (Array.isArray(value.limits)) {
+    for (const limit of value.limits) {
+      if (isObject(limit) && typeof limit.reason === "string") reasons.push(limit.reason);
+    }
+  }
+  if (isObject(value.stop) && typeof value.stop.reason === "string") reasons.push(value.stop.reason);
+  for (const [key, child] of Object.entries(value)) {
+    if (key !== "limits" && key !== "stop") reasons.push(...collectLimitReasons(child));
+  }
+  return reasons;
+}
+
+export function matchAnswer(answer: unknown, expect: Expectation): Mismatch[] {
+  const failures: Mismatch[] = [];
+  for (const [rule, checks] of [["includes", expect.includes], ["excludes", expect.excludes]] as const) {
+    for (const check of checks) {
+      const actual = selectPath(answer, check.path);
+      const found = actual.some(value => isObject(value) && value.file === check.file && value.line === check.line);
+      if (found !== (rule === "includes")) failures.push({
+        path: check.path, expected: { [rule]: { file: check.file, line: check.line } },
+        actual, message: `${rule} location check failed`,
+      });
+    }
+  }
+  for (const check of expect.equals) {
+    const selected = selectPath(answer, check.path);
+    const actual = check.path.includes("[]") || check.path.split(".").includes("children") ? selected : selected[0];
+    if (!isDeepStrictEqual(actual, check.value)) failures.push({
+      path: check.path, expected: check.value, actual: actual === undefined ? { missing: true } : actual,
+      message: "equals check failed",
+    });
+  }
+  if (expect.ambiguous !== null) {
+    const actual = isObject(answer) ? answer.ambiguous : undefined;
+    if (actual !== expect.ambiguous) failures.push({ path: "ambiguous", expected: expect.ambiguous,
+      actual: actual ?? { missing: true }, message: "ambiguous check failed" });
+  }
+  const reasons = collectLimitReasons(answer);
+  for (const reason of expect.limitReasons) {
+    if (!reasons.includes(reason)) failures.push({ path: "limits/stop", expected: reason, actual: reasons,
+      message: "limit reason missing" });
+  }
+  return failures;
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/process.ts b/code_map/eval/process.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..32b058b2f2be1ec113969c7a57a3f9b9da6974c6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/process.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+import { createHash } from "node:crypto";
+import { lstat, readFile, readlink, readdir } from "node:fs/promises";
+import { join } from "node:path";
+
+export type ProcessResult = { exitCode: number; stdout: string; stderr: string; command: string[] };
+export type FileSnapshot = Record<string, string>;
+export type FileChange = { path: string; change: "added" | "removed" | "modified" };
+
+export function shellQuote(value: string): string { return "'" + value.replaceAll("'", "'\\''") + "'"; }
+
+export async function captureProcess(command: string[], cwd: string): Promise<ProcessResult> {
+  try {
+    const child = Bun.spawn(command, { cwd, stdout: "pipe", stderr: "pipe", stdin: "ignore" });
+    const [exitCode, stdout, stderr] = await Promise.all([child.exited, new Response(child.stdout).text(), new Response(child.stderr).text()]);
+    return { exitCode, stdout, stderr, command };
+  } catch (error) {
+    return { exitCode: -1, stdout: "", stderr: String(error), command };
+  }
+}
+
+export async function snapshotFiles(roots: string[]): Promise<FileSnapshot> {
+  const snapshot: FileSnapshot = {};
+  async function visit(path: string) {
+    if (Object.hasOwn(snapshot, path)) return;
+    const stat = await lstat(path, { bigint: true });
+    const metadata = `${stat.mode}:${stat.size}:${stat.mtimeNs}:${stat.ctimeNs}`;
+    if (stat.isSymbolicLink()) snapshot[path] = `symlink:${metadata}:${await readlink(path)}`;
+    else if (stat.isDirectory()) {
+      snapshot[path] = `directory:${stat.mode}:${stat.mtimeNs}:${stat.ctimeNs}`;
+      for (const entry of (await readdir(path)).sort()) await visit(join(path, entry));
+    } else if (stat.isFile()) snapshot[path] = `file:${metadata}:${createHash("sha256").update(await readFile(path)).digest("hex")}`;
+    else snapshot[path] = `other:${metadata}`;
+  }
+  for (const root of [...new Set(roots)].sort()) await visit(root);
+  return snapshot;
+}
+
+export function compareSnapshots(before: FileSnapshot, after: FileSnapshot): FileChange[] {
+  return [...new Set([...Object.keys(before), ...Object.keys(after)])].sort().flatMap(path => {
+    if (before[path] === after[path]) return [];
+    const change = before[path] === undefined ? "added" : after[path] === undefined ? "removed" : "modified";
+    return [{ path, change }];
+  });
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/report.ts b/code_map/eval/report.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..27adc7333d30648fc27a257e19366d8baead01c0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/report.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+import { requirementLines, uncheckedParts, type Requirement, type Status } from "./requirements.ts";
+import type { Mismatch } from "./matcher.ts";
+import type { ProcessResult, FileChange } from "./process.ts";
+
+export type CaseResult = {
+  id: string; source: string; requirement: Requirement; line: string; args: string[];
+  status: Status; reasons: string[]; failures: Mismatch[]; answer: unknown;
+  process: ProcessResult; isolation: boolean; changedFiles: FileChange[]; markerCreated?: boolean;
+};
+export type Observation = { id: string; requirement: Requirement; line: string; status: Status; reason?: string };
+
+export function aggregateStatus(statuses: Status[]): Status {
+  if (statuses.includes("NOT MET")) return "NOT MET";
+  if (!statuses.length || statuses.includes("NOT CHECKED")) return "NOT CHECKED";
+  return "MET";
+}
+
+function totals(statuses: Status[]) {
+  return Object.fromEntries((["MET", "NOT MET", "NOT CHECKED"] as const).map(status => [status, statuses.filter(item => item === status).length]));
+}
+
+export function buildReport(cases: CaseResult[], observations: Observation[], isolationProbe: ProcessResult) {
+  const requirements = Object.entries(requirementLines).map(([requirement, lines]) => {
+    const checks = lines.map(line => {
+      const casesForLine = cases.filter(result => result.requirement === requirement && result.line === line);
+      const observationsForLine = observations.filter(result => result.requirement === requirement && result.line === line);
+      const status = aggregateStatus([...casesForLine.map(result => result.status), ...observationsForLine.map(result => result.status)]);
+      const reasons = [...casesForLine.flatMap(result => result.reasons), ...observationsForLine.flatMap(result => result.reason ? [result.reason] : [])];
+      if (!casesForLine.length && !observationsForLine.length) reasons.push(requirement === "A6" ? "No opencode case files for the three modules were supplied." : requirement === "L2" ? "P5 measures cost against reading; this evaluator does not measure L2." : "No case exercises this Fails-if line.");
+      return { line, status, caseIds: casesForLine.map(result => result.id), observations: observationsForLine, reasons };
+    });
+    return { requirement, status: aggregateStatus(checks.map(check => check.status)), lines: checks };
+  });
+  return {
+    checker: "P2 Codex evaluator; authored independently of the future tool builder",
+    scope: "MET records the fixture/case checks assigned to this evaluator, not a proof for all repositories. Canned-stub results test the evaluator, not a real code-map tool.",
+    requirements, cases, uncheckedParts, isolationProbe,
+    totals: { requirements: totals(requirements.map(item => item.status)),
+      lines: totals(requirements.flatMap(item => item.lines.map(line => line.status))), cases: totals(cases.map(result => result.status)) },
+  };
+}
+
+export type Report = ReturnType<typeof buildReport>;
+
+export function renderReport(report: Report): string {
+  const rows = ["# Code-map evaluation", "", report.checker, "", report.scope, "", "| Requirement | Status |", "|---|---|"];
+  for (const requirement of report.requirements) rows.push(`| ${requirement.requirement} | ${requirement.status} |`);
+  rows.push("", "## Fails-if lines", "");
+  for (const requirement of report.requirements) {
+    for (const line of requirement.lines) {
+      rows.push(`- **${requirement.requirement} ${line.status}** — ${line.line}. Cases: ${line.caseIds.join(", ") || "none"}.`);
+      for (const reason of [...new Set(line.reasons)]) rows.push(`  - ${reason}`);
+    }
+  }
+  rows.push("", "## Failures", "");
+  for (const result of report.cases.filter(result => result.status === "NOT MET")) {
+    rows.push(`### ${result.id} (${result.requirement})`, "", `Case file: ${result.source}`, "", `Arguments: \`${JSON.stringify(result.args)}\``, "",
+      `Exit: ${result.process.exitCode}. Isolation: ${result.isolation}.`, "", "```json", JSON.stringify(result.failures, null, 2), "```", "",
+      "Tool stdout:", "```text", result.process.stdout, "```", "Tool stderr:", "```text", result.process.stderr, "```", "");
+  }
+  rows.push("## Parts not checked", "");
+  for (const part of report.uncheckedParts) rows.push(`- **${part.requirement} ${part.status}** — ${part.reason}`);
+  rows.push("", "## Totals", "", "```json", JSON.stringify(report.totals, null, 2), "```", "");
+  return rows.join("\n");
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/requirements.ts b/code_map/eval/requirements.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..631998d2ae0470e7e718fb6705d2a4f7a690ff5c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/requirements.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+export const requirementLines = {
+  R1: ["mapping a fixture whose top level writes a marker creates that marker"],
+  R2: [
+    "an implementation the lookup finds has no link",
+    "a declaration is presented as proof of an implementation",
+    "a test fake is unlabelled or presented as the real implementation",
+    "an unresolved or ambiguous target is unmarked",
+  ],
+  R3: ["protected content leaves the machine or enters git"],
+  A1: ["a claim lacks its location or contradicts the code, or a checked example misses a known item"],
+  A2: [
+    "a known place is not found",
+    "an ambiguous match is treated as certain, or a candidate not built is not named",
+    "a known link within the depth is missing, or a shown link contradicts the code",
+    "a link lacks its kind or location",
+    "a function reached twice is shown twice",
+  ],
+  A3: [
+    "the count differs from the list, or a link lacks its evidence",
+    "a test with a known path is missing",
+    "static links are called coverage",
+    "the per-function file report runs without the user's request",
+  ],
+  A5: ["an answer comes only inside a dump or without its evidence or limits, or a whole map is produced unasked"],
+  A6: ["fewer than three modules are mapped, or a map fails A1"],
+  L1: ["a branch stops early without a reason, or an empty result is presented as proof of absence"],
+  L2: ["it leaves out correctness, the build cost, the reading tokens or the time, or hides a worse result"],
+} as const;
+
+export type Requirement = keyof typeof requirementLines;
+export type Status = "MET" | "NOT MET" | "NOT CHECKED";
+
+export const uncheckedParts = [
+  { requirement: "A2", status: "NOT CHECKED", reason: "P6 checks the agent's selection and naming of candidates it did not build." },
+  { requirement: "A3", status: "NOT CHECKED", reason: "P6 checks whether the agent asks the user before requesting a per-function file report." },
+  { requirement: "A5", status: "NOT CHECKED", reason: "P6 checks whether the agent requests a whole map without being asked." },
+  { requirement: "R3", status: "NOT CHECKED", reason: "Network isolation and filesystem snapshots do not establish absence of caught connection attempts, transmission by other processes, or downstream training use." },
+] as const;
diff --git a/code_map/eval/run.ts b/code_map/eval/run.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5b1165f060188e0779a400c1d2e13175b2b02034
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/run.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@
+import { mkdir, rm, writeFile } from "node:fs/promises";
+import { resolve } from "node:path";
+import { loadCaseFile, type LoadedCaseFile, type EvalCase } from "./case-file.ts";
+import { validateAnswer } from "./contract.ts";
+import { matchAnswer, type Mismatch } from "./matcher.ts";
+import { captureProcess, compareSnapshots, shellQuote, snapshotFiles, type ProcessResult } from "./process.ts";
+import { buildReport, renderReport, type CaseResult, type Observation } from "./report.ts";
+import { requirementLines } from "./requirements.ts";
+
+export type EvalOptions = { tool: string; cases: string[]; out: string; cwd?: string };
+
+export function parseArguments(args: string[]): EvalOptions {
+  let tool = ""; let out = ""; const cases: string[] = [];
+  for (let index = 0; index < args.length; index++) {
+    const flag = args[index]; const value = args[++index];
+    if (!value || !["--tool", "--cases", "--out"].includes(flag!)) throw new Error("Usage: bun eval/run.ts --tool <command> [--cases <file>]... --out <dir>");
+    if (flag === "--tool") tool = value;
+    else if (flag === "--out") out = value;
+    else cases.push(value);
+  }
+  if (!tool.trim() || !out) throw new Error("--tool and --out are required");
+  if (!cases.length) cases.push(resolve(import.meta.dir, "cases/fixtures.json"));
+  return { tool, out: resolve(out), cases };
+}
+
+export function toolArguments(file: LoadedCaseFile, test: EvalCase): string[] {
+  return [...test.args, ...file.project.flatMap(project => ["--project", project]), "--root", file.root,
+    ...file.tests.flatMap(pattern => ["--tests", pattern]), "--json"];
+}
+
+async function evaluateCase(options: EvalOptions, file: LoadedCaseFile, test: EvalCase, probe: ProcessResult): Promise<CaseResult> {
+  const cwd = options.cwd ?? process.cwd();
+  const args = toolArguments(file, test);
+  const marker = file.root === resolve(import.meta.dir, "fixtures") ? resolve(file.root, "marker/EXECUTED.marker") : undefined;
+  if (marker) await rm(marker, { force: true });
+  const before = await snapshotFiles([file.root, cwd]);
+  const command = `${options.tool} ${args.map(shellQuote).join(" ")}`;
+  const isolation = probe.exitCode === 0;
+  const processResult = await captureProcess(isolation ? ["unshare", "-rn", "--", "sh", "-c", command] : ["sh", "-c", command], cwd);
+  const after = await snapshotFiles([file.root, cwd]);
+  const changedFiles = compareSnapshots(before, after);
+  const markerCreated = marker ? await Bun.file(marker).exists() : undefined;
+  if (marker) await rm(marker, { force: true });
+  const failures: Mismatch[] = [];
+  let answer: unknown = null;
+  if (processResult.exitCode !== 0) failures.push({ path: "$process.exitCode", expected: 0, actual: processResult.exitCode, message: processResult.stderr });
+  try {
+    answer = JSON.parse(processResult.stdout);
+    failures.push(...matchAnswer(answer, test.expect), ...validateAnswer(answer, test.args, file.tests));
+  } catch (error) {
+    failures.push({ path: "$stdout", expected: "one JSON Answer", actual: processResult.stdout, message: String(error) });
+  }
+  if (changedFiles.length) failures.push({ path: "$filesystem", expected: "no writes under root or working directory", actual: changedFiles, message: "R3 filesystem changed" });
+  if (markerCreated) failures.push({ path: "$marker", expected: "marker absent", actual: marker, message: "R1 repository source was executed" });
+  const reasons: string[] = [];
+  if (test.requirement === "R3" && !isolation) reasons.push(`unshare -rn unavailable (exit ${probe.exitCode}): ${probe.stderr.trim()}`);
+  if (test.requirement === "R1" && !marker) reasons.push("The case format has no marker path; only the bundled marker fixture has a runtime R1 check.");
+  const status = failures.length ? "NOT MET" : reasons.length ? "NOT CHECKED" : "MET";
+  return { id: test.id, source: file.source, requirement: test.requirement, line: test.line,
+    args, status, reasons, failures, answer, process: processResult, isolation, changedFiles, markerCreated };
+}
+
+export async function evaluate(options: EvalOptions) {
+  const files = await Promise.all(options.cases.map(loadCaseFile));
+  const probe = await captureProcess(["unshare", "-rn", "--", "true"], options.cwd ?? process.cwd());
+  const results: CaseResult[] = [];
+  const observations: Observation[] = [];
+  // Sequential runs make before/after snapshots attributable to one tool invocation.
+  for (const file of files) for (const test of file.cases) {
+    const result = await evaluateCase(options, file, test, probe);
+    results.push(result);
+    observations.push({ id: result.id, requirement: "R3", line: requirementLines.R3[0],
+      status: result.changedFiles.length ? "NOT MET" : probe.exitCode !== 0 ? "NOT CHECKED" : result.process.exitCode !== 0 ? "NOT MET" : "MET",
+      reason: probe.exitCode !== 0 ? `unshare -rn unavailable (exit ${probe.exitCode}): ${probe.stderr.trim()}` :
+        result.changedFiles.length ? "Tool changed files under root or working directory; see case evidence." :
+        result.process.exitCode !== 0 ? "Tool failed under network isolation; exit and output retained in case evidence." : undefined });
+  }
+  const moduleSuffixes = ["packages/core/src/session", "packages/core/src/tool", "packages/ai"];
+  const matchingA1Maps = results.filter(result => result.requirement === "A1" && result.args[0] === "map");
+  const moduleChecks = moduleSuffixes.map(suffix => matchingA1Maps.filter(result =>
+    result.args.some(arg => arg.replaceAll("\\", "/").replace(/\/$/, "").endsWith(suffix)) &&
+    (suffix !== "packages/core/src/tool" || result.args.some(arg => arg.replaceAll("\\", "/").endsWith("packages/core/src/permission.ts")))));
+  const allModulesChecked = moduleChecks.every(checks => checks.length > 0);
+  const allModulesMet = allModulesChecked && moduleChecks.every(checks => checks.every(check => check.status === "MET"));
+  for (const result of results.filter(result => result.requirement === "A6")) {
+    if (result.status === "NOT MET") continue;
+    if (!allModulesChecked) {
+      result.status = "NOT CHECKED";
+      result.reasons.push("A6 needs A1 map checks for all three opencode modules, including tool with permission.ts.");
+    } else if (!allModulesMet) {
+      result.status = "NOT MET";
+      result.failures.push({ path: "$A6", expected: "A1 passes for all three opencode module maps", actual: moduleChecks, message: "A module map failed A1" });
+    }
+  }
+  if (allModulesChecked) observations.push({ id: "A6-three-module-A1-checks", requirement: "A6", line: requirementLines.A6[0],
+    status: allModulesMet ? "MET" : "NOT MET", reason: "A6 is derived from A1 cases for the three specified opencode module-map commands." });
+  const report = buildReport(results, observations, probe);
+  await mkdir(options.out, { recursive: true });
+  await writeFile(resolve(options.out, "report.json"), JSON.stringify(report, null, 2) + "\n");
+  await writeFile(resolve(options.out, "report.md"), renderReport(report));
+  return report;
+}
+
+if (import.meta.main) {
+  try {
+    const options = parseArguments(Bun.argv.slice(2));
+    const report = await evaluate(options);
+    console.log("Requirements:", JSON.stringify(report.totals.requirements));
+    console.log("Fails-if lines:", JSON.stringify(report.totals.lines));
+    console.log("Cases:", JSON.stringify(report.totals.cases));
+    console.log("Report:", resolve(options.out, "report.json"));
+    if (report.cases.some(result => result.status === "NOT MET")) process.exitCode = 1;
+  } catch (error) {
+    console.error(String(error)); process.exitCode = 2;
+  }
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/stub/stub.ts b/code_map/eval/stub/stub.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..98b4d1f347ef9d7a120bcfd70599f61ee7a79775
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/stub/stub.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+import { readFile } from "node:fs/promises";
+import { resolve } from "node:path";
+import { isDeepStrictEqual } from "node:util";
+import { loadCaseFile } from "../case-file.ts";
+import { toolArguments } from "../run.ts";
+
+const file = await loadCaseFile(resolve(import.meta.dir, "../cases/fixtures.json"));
+const args = Bun.argv.slice(2);
+const matching = file.cases.filter(test => isDeepStrictEqual(toolArguments(file, test), args));
+if (!matching.length) {
+  console.log(JSON.stringify({ command: args[0] ?? "", limits: [], empty: "none found by static analysis" }));
+} else {
+  const answers = await Promise.all(matching.map(test => readFile(resolve(import.meta.dir, "answers", test.id + ".json"), "utf8")));
+  const answer: unknown = JSON.parse(answers[0]!);
+  // Several checks can ask the same question; breaking any of their canned files must be visible.
+  if (answers.some(text => !isDeepStrictEqual(JSON.parse(text), answer))) {
+    throw new Error(`Conflicting canned answers for identical command: ${matching.map(test => test.id).join(", ")}`);
+  }
+  console.log(JSON.stringify(answer));
+}

diff --git a/code_map/eval/README.md b/code_map/eval/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7312015d7028aaedd071ff319a2976ccef47320d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Evaluator
+
+From `code_map/`:
+
+```sh
+bun eval/run.ts --tool "bun eval/stub/stub.ts" --cases eval/cases/fixtures.json --out /tmp/cm-eval
+```
+
+From the repository root, the bundled case paths work unchanged:
+
+```sh
+bun code_map/eval/run.ts --tool "bun code_map/eval/stub/stub.ts" --out /tmp/cm-eval
+```
+
+Additional `--cases` files follow the spec's format. The shell tool command is trusted; appended case arguments are shell quoted. Paths in external case files are relative to the invoking working directory. The evaluator reads JSON stdout and preserves the full command, exit status, stdout, stderr, changed-file list and expectation mismatches in `report.json`. `report.md` presents the requirement/line statuses and failures. Runs are sequential so snapshots belong to one invocation.
+
+The 34 fixture cases exercise the 18 fixture-checkable Fails-if lines, with runtime marker checks and R3 observations on every invocation. A6 and L2 are NOT CHECKED without the external evaluation work. The report also states the agent/privacy parts it cannot establish. See [SPEC_QUESTIONS.md](SPEC_QUESTIONS.md).
+
+`stub/answers/<case-id>.json` contains each editable canned answer. Change a location, resolution, count, limit, or fake label and rerun: the evaluator should report NOT MET. Identical commands have identical canned files; the stub rejects disagreement among them, so changing any one is observable. Unknown commands print the empty static-analysis answer required by the brief.
+
+These checks were written by P2 Codex independently of the future builder. Passing the stub validates evaluator plumbing and its known answers. It does not establish correctness of a future tool on other source projects.
diff --git a/code_map/eval/SPEC_QUESTIONS.md b/code_map/eval/SPEC_QUESTIONS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d596680343c0e10ae2125ece2a261c721798ab07
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/SPEC_QUESTIONS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Spec questions and evaluator scope
+
+Author: P2 Codex. These are implementation readings, not changes to the requirements or spec.
+
+| Question | Narrow reading used |
+|---|---|
+| What makes a relative case-file path relative? | External case `root` and `project` paths are relative to the evaluator's working directory, following the example's `root: "."`. The bundled fixture case file uses package-relative paths so the two invocation forms in the brief both work. `--cases` itself is relative to the working directory. |
+| How does `equals` work with `[]` or recursive `children`? | A simple path compares its single selected value. A path using `[]` or `children` compares the complete selected list, in traversal order. An absent simple path is missing, not JSON `null`; an empty wildcard selection is `[]`. `children` visits descendants in source/depth-first order, never the current step. |
+| What happens for `tests --file` without `--per-function`? | The tool may give an empty JSON answer with an explanatory limit; it must not return a per-function report. The fixture does not prescribe the explanation's wording. The spec defines no positive per-function JSON shape, so the evaluator does not invent one. |
+| What are evaluator exit codes? | 0 means a report completed without NOT MET cases; NOT CHECKED is allowed. 1 means NOT MET cases. 2 means invalid evaluator input or an evaluator/environment failure. |
+| Where is the R1 marker path for external cases? | The case format has no marker field. Runtime marker checks use only the known bundled `marker/EXECUTED.marker`, after every invocation (including the four required commands). An external R1 case alone is NOT CHECKED for the runtime part. The evaluator removes only its own marker. |
+| Does `unshare -rn` detect connection attempts? | It isolates network access; it does not trace syscalls. Nonzero tool exit and filesystem changes fail the bounded check. A connection failure caught inside a successful tool cannot be detected from stdout. Such attempts and the broader privacy/training promise remain explicitly NOT CHECKED in `uncheckedParts`. No syscall tracer dependency is introduced. |
+| Does isolation establish all of R3? | No. R3's MET line describes the spec-assigned isolation and before/after filesystem observation only. Snapshots hash regular files and retain mode, timestamps and symlink targets under `--root` and cwd; links are not followed. Files outside those trees, transient changes restored between snapshots, and transmissions by other processes are not observed. A missing/denied `unshare` makes R3 NOT CHECKED, even if snapshots are unchanged. |
+| How are combined tool/agent Fails-if lines reported? | Line statuses describe the evaluator's tool checks. `uncheckedParts` separately records A2 candidate choice/naming, A3 asking the user, and A5 whether the user asked. These belong to P6; a MET tool line does not assert that the agent part passed. |
+| Can a fixture check A6 or L2? | No. No A6 claim is made without external cases for the three real opencode modules. L2 is P5's independent comparison. Both remain NOT CHECKED in the bundled suite. |
+| How does an external case certify A6? | The spec supplies no module-certification field or A1 linkage field. An A6 case is therefore NOT CHECKED unless the three module-map commands and A1 case checks on those same commands are present; module location is identified by the three specified path suffixes. |
+
+Requirements check: **who decides**, **one thing**, **unit**, **can it fail**, **weak words**, **level**, **basis**, and **links** pass for the concrete evaluator contract when read as the author's accepted spec and fixture checks. The unresolved interface details above affect **who decides** or **can it fail**; the brief explicitly assigns their recording and the narrowest reading to this evaluator. No numeric threshold, acceptance criterion, or new dependency is added.
diff --git a/code_map/eval/case-file.ts b/code_map/eval/case-file.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..405543c2ccf065ae61f3b1641dec03908f5f2fea
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/case-file.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+import { readFile } from "node:fs/promises";
+import { resolve } from "node:path";
+import { isObject, selectPath, type Expectation } from "./matcher.ts";
+import { requirementLines, type Requirement } from "./requirements.ts";
+
+export type EvalCase = { id: string; requirement: Requirement; line: string; args: string[]; expect: Expectation };
+export type CaseFile = { project: string[]; root: string; tests: string[]; cases: EvalCase[] };
+export type LoadedCaseFile = CaseFile & { source: string };
+
+function stringArray(value: unknown): value is string[] {
+  return Array.isArray(value) && value.every(item => typeof item === "string");
+}
+
+export function validateCaseFile(value: unknown): CaseFile {
+  if (!isObject(value) || !stringArray(value.project) || !value.project.length ||
+      typeof value.root !== "string" || !stringArray(value.tests) || !Array.isArray(value.cases)) {
+    throw new Error("Case file needs project: string[], root: string, tests: string[], cases: array");
+  }
+  const ids = new Set<string>();
+  for (const candidate of value.cases) {
+    if (!isObject(candidate) || typeof candidate.id !== "string" || !candidate.id || ids.has(candidate.id) ||
+        typeof candidate.requirement !== "string" || !(candidate.requirement in requirementLines) ||
+        typeof candidate.line !== "string" || !stringArray(candidate.args) || !candidate.args.length || !isObject(candidate.expect)) {
+      throw new Error("Invalid or duplicate case: " + JSON.stringify(candidate));
+    }
+    ids.add(candidate.id);
+    const lines: readonly string[] = requirementLines[candidate.requirement as Requirement];
+    if (!lines.includes(candidate.line.replace(/\.$/, ""))) throw new Error(`Unknown Fails-if line in ${candidate.id}: ${candidate.line}`);
+    candidate.line = candidate.line.replace(/\.$/, "");
+    const expect = candidate.expect;
+    if (!Array.isArray(expect.includes) || !Array.isArray(expect.excludes) || !Array.isArray(expect.equals) ||
+        ![true, false, null].includes(expect.ambiguous as boolean | null) || !stringArray(expect.limitReasons)) {
+      throw new Error(`Invalid expectation in ${candidate.id}`);
+    }
+    for (const location of [...expect.includes, ...expect.excludes]) {
+      if (!isObject(location) || typeof location.path !== "string" || typeof location.file !== "string" ||
+          !Number.isInteger(location.line) || (location.line as number) < 1) throw new Error(`Invalid location in ${candidate.id}`);
+      selectPath({}, location.path);
+    }
+    for (const equality of expect.equals) {
+      if (!isObject(equality) || typeof equality.path !== "string" || !Object.hasOwn(equality, "value")) {
+        throw new Error(`Invalid equality in ${candidate.id}`);
+      }
+      selectPath({}, equality.path);
+    }
+  }
+  return value as CaseFile;
+}
+
+export async function loadCaseFile(path: string): Promise<LoadedCaseFile> {
+  const source = resolve(path);
+  const value = validateCaseFile(JSON.parse(await readFile(source, "utf8")));
+  // Bundled examples remain runnable from either the repository or the package directory.
+  const base = source === resolve(import.meta.dir, "cases/fixtures.json") ? resolve(import.meta.dir, "..") : process.cwd();
+  return { ...value, source, root: resolve(base, value.root), project: value.project.map(project => resolve(base, project)) };
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/contract.ts b/code_map/eval/contract.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cdc73c588b836def841737343bd78ee33281b0c4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/contract.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,181 @@
+import { isObject, type Mismatch } from "./matcher.ts";
+
+const nodeKinds = ["function", "method", "arrow", "effect-fn", "property", "class", "variable", "interface-member", "other"];
+const limitKinds = ["depth", "dynamic", "outside-repo", "other-process", "not-found", "seen", "other"];
+const stepKinds = ["call", "if", "else", "loop", "try", "catch", "return", "yield*"];
+
+export function validateAnswer(answer: unknown, args: string[], testPatterns: string[]): Mismatch[] {
+  const failures: Mismatch[] = [];
+  const fail = (path: string, expected: unknown, actual: unknown) => failures.push({ path, expected,
+    actual: actual === undefined ? { missing: true } : actual, message: "JSON contract violated" });
+  function location(value: unknown, path: string): value is Record<string, unknown> {
+    if (!isObject(value) || typeof value.file !== "string" || !value.file || value.file.startsWith("/") ||
+        !Number.isInteger(value.line) || (value.line as number) < 1 ||
+        (value.endLine !== undefined && (!Number.isInteger(value.endLine) || (value.endLine as number) < (value.line as number)))) {
+      fail(path, "relative file and positive 1-based line (endLine >= line)", value); return false;
+    }
+    return true;
+  }
+  function node(value: unknown, path: string): value is Record<string, unknown> {
+    if (!location(value, path)) return false;
+    if (typeof value.name !== "string" || !value.name || !nodeKinds.includes(value.kind as string)) {
+      fail(path, "named Node with a spec kind", value); return false;
+    }
+    return true;
+  }
+  function limit(value: unknown, path: string) {
+    if (!isObject(value) || !limitKinds.includes(value.reason as string)) { fail(path, "Limit with stated reason", value); return; }
+    if (value.at !== undefined) location(value.at, path + ".at");
+    if (value.ref !== undefined) location(value.ref, path + ".ref");
+    if (value.reason === "seen" && value.ref === undefined) fail(path, "seen limit with ref", value);
+    if (value.reason === "other" && (typeof value.text !== "string" || !value.text.trim())) fail(path, "other limit with text", value);
+  }
+  function array(value: unknown, path: string, visit: (item: unknown, path: string) => void) {
+    if (!Array.isArray(value)) { fail(path, "array", value); return; }
+    value.forEach((item, index) => visit(item, `${path}[${index}]`));
+  }
+  function link(value: unknown, path: string) {
+    if (!isObject(value)) { fail(path, "Link", value); return; }
+    node(value.from, path + ".from"); location(value.site, path + ".site");
+    if (!["call", "new", "service-call"].includes(value.kind as string)) fail(path + ".kind", "call | new | service-call", value.kind);
+    if (!["definition", "implementation-lookup"].includes(value.via as string)) fail(path + ".via", "definition | implementation-lookup", value.via);
+    if (value.declaration !== undefined) location(value.declaration, path + ".declaration");
+    array(value.candidates, path + ".candidates", (candidate, at) => {
+      if (!node(candidate, at)) return;
+      const testFake = testPatterns.some(pattern => new Bun.Glob(pattern).match(candidate.file as string));
+      if (candidate.testFake !== testFake) fail(at + ".testFake", testFake, candidate.testFake);
+    });
+    const real = Array.isArray(value.candidates) ? value.candidates.filter(candidate => isObject(candidate) && candidate.testFake === false) : [];
+    const expectedResolution = real.length === 0 ? "unresolved" : real.length === 1 ? "implementation" : "ambiguous";
+    if (value.resolution !== expectedResolution) fail(path + ".resolution", expectedResolution, value.resolution);
+    if (value.resolution === "implementation") {
+      if (node(value.to, path + ".to")) {
+        const target = value.to;
+        if (!real.some(candidate => candidate.file === target.file && candidate.line === target.line)) {
+          fail(path + ".to", "the sole non-test candidate", value.to);
+        }
+        if (value.to.kind === "interface-member" || (value.via === "implementation-lookup" && isObject(value.declaration) &&
+            value.to.file === value.declaration.file && value.to.line === value.declaration.line)) {
+          fail(path + ".to", "an implementation, rather than its interface declaration", value.to);
+        }
+      }
+    } else if (value.to !== undefined) fail(path + ".to", "absent for unresolved or ambiguous links", value.to);
+    if (value.resolution === "unresolved" && (typeof value.reason !== "string" || !value.reason.trim())) fail(path + ".reason", "unresolved reason", value.reason);
+  }
+  function flowStep(value: unknown, path: string) {
+    if (!isObject(value)) { fail(path, "Step", value); return; }
+    location(value.at, path + ".at");
+    if (!stepKinds.includes(value.kind as string)) fail(path + ".kind", stepKinds, value.kind);
+    if (typeof value.text !== "string" || !value.text.trim()) fail(path + ".text", "full source text", value.text);
+    if (value.children !== undefined) array(value.children, path + ".children", flowStep);
+  }
+  if (!isObject(answer)) { fail("$", "Answer object", answer); return failures; }
+  const fields = ["command", "query", "ambiguous", "matches", "links", "chain", "tests", "map", "limits", "empty"];
+  for (const key of Object.keys(answer)) if (!fields.includes(key)) fail(key, "specified Answer fields only", answer[key]);
+  if (answer.command !== args[0]) fail("command", args[0], answer.command);
+  array(answer.limits, "limits", limit);
+  if (answer.query !== undefined && (!Array.isArray(answer.query) || !answer.query.every(query => typeof query === "string"))) fail("query", "string[]", answer.query);
+  if (answer.empty !== undefined && answer.empty !== "none found by static analysis") fail("empty", "none found by static analysis", answer.empty);
+  if (args[0] !== "map" && answer.map !== undefined) fail("map", "absent for a specific question", answer.map);
+  if (answer.matches !== undefined) {
+    array(answer.matches, "matches", node);
+    if (Array.isArray(answer.matches) && answer.ambiguous !== (answer.matches.length > 1)) fail("ambiguous", answer.matches.length > 1, answer.ambiguous);
+    if (answer.ambiguous === true && args[0] !== "find" && args[0] !== "where" &&
+        [answer.links, answer.chain, answer.tests, answer.map].some(value => value !== undefined)) fail("$", "ambiguous name: candidates only", answer);
+  }
+  if (answer.links !== undefined) array(answer.links, "links", link);
+  if (answer.chain !== undefined) {
+    if (!isObject(answer.chain)) fail("chain", "{up, down}", answer.chain);
+    else for (const direction of ["up", "down"] as const) {
+      const depthFlag = args.indexOf("--" + direction);
+      const depth = depthFlag < 0 ? 6 : Number(args[depthFlag + 1]);
+      const expanded = new Set<string>();
+      const rootMatch = /^(.*):(\d+)$/.exec(args[1] ?? "");
+      if (rootMatch) expanded.add(`${rootMatch[1]}:${rootMatch[2]}`);
+      function chainStep(value: unknown, path: string, level: number) {
+        if (!isObject(value)) { fail(path, "ChainStep", value); return; }
+        if (value.level !== level || level > depth) fail(path + ".level", `level ${level}, at most ${depth}`, value.level);
+        link(value.link, path + ".link");
+        if (value.stop !== undefined) limit(value.stop, path + ".stop");
+        const target = isObject(value.link) ? value.link[direction === "down" ? "to" : "from"] : undefined;
+        if (isObject(target)) {
+          const key = `${target.file}:${target.line}`;
+          if (expanded.has(key)) {
+            if (!isObject(value.stop) || value.stop.reason !== "seen" || !isObject(value.stop.ref) ||
+                value.stop.ref.file !== target.file || value.stop.ref.line !== target.line) fail(path + ".stop", "seen with reference to first occurrence", value.stop);
+          } else {
+            if (isObject(value.stop) && value.stop.reason === "seen") fail(path + ".stop", "reference to an already shown function", value.stop);
+            expanded.add(key);
+          }
+        }
+        if (Array.isArray(value.children) && value.children.length && value.stop !== undefined) fail(path + ".children", "no expansion after a stop", value.children);
+        if (level === depth && value.stop === undefined) fail(path + ".stop", "depth stop", value.stop);
+        array(value.children, path + ".children", (child, at) => chainStep(child, at, level + 1));
+      }
+      array(answer.chain[direction], `chain.${direction}`, (step, at) => chainStep(step, at, 1));
+    }
+  }
+  if (answer.tests !== undefined) {
+    if (args.includes("--file") && !args.includes("--per-function")) fail("tests", "absent without --per-function", answer.tests);
+    if (!isObject(answer.tests)) fail("tests", "TestsAnswer", answer.tests);
+    else {
+      if (answer.tests.label !== "static-call-path") fail("tests.label", "static-call-path", answer.tests.label);
+      if (!Array.isArray(answer.tests.tests) || answer.tests.count !== answer.tests.tests.length) fail("tests.count", Array.isArray(answer.tests.tests) ? answer.tests.tests.length : "tests.length", answer.tests.count);
+      const testCase = (value: unknown, path: string) => {
+        if (!location(value, path)) return;
+        if (typeof value.name !== "string" || !value.name.trim()) fail(path + ".name", "test case name", value.name);
+        if (!Array.isArray(value.path) || !value.path.length) fail(path + ".path", "nonempty evidence path", value.path);
+        array(value.path, path + ".path", link);
+        const throughFake = Array.isArray(value.path) && value.path.some(edge => isObject(edge) && edge.kind === "service-call" &&
+          Array.isArray(edge.candidates) && edge.candidates.some(candidate => isObject(candidate) && candidate.testFake === true));
+        if (value.throughFake !== throughFake) fail(path + ".throughFake", throughFake, value.throughFake);
+        if (Array.isArray(value.path)) for (let index = 1; index < value.path.length; index++) {
+          const previous = value.path[index - 1]; const next = value.path[index];
+          if (isObject(previous) && isObject(previous.to) && isObject(next) && isObject(next.from) &&
+              (previous.to.file !== next.from.file || previous.to.line !== next.from.line)) fail(path + ".path", "connected static call path", value.path);
+        }
+      };
+      array(answer.tests.tests, "tests.tests", testCase);
+      array(answer.tests.undecided, "tests.undecided", testCase);
+      const fakeFlag = args.indexOf("--fake-rule"); const rule = fakeFlag < 0 ? undefined : args[fakeFlag + 1];
+      const countedFakes = Array.isArray(answer.tests.tests) && answer.tests.tests.some(test => isObject(test) && test.throughFake === true);
+      if (rule !== "count" && countedFakes) fail("tests.tests", "fakes counted only with --fake-rule count", answer.tests.tests);
+      if (rule !== undefined && Array.isArray(answer.tests.undecided) && answer.tests.undecided.length) fail("tests.undecided", [], answer.tests.undecided);
+      if (rule === undefined && Array.isArray(answer.tests.undecided) && answer.tests.undecided.length &&
+          (!Array.isArray(answer.limits) || !answer.limits.some(limit => isObject(limit) && limit.reason === "other" && limit.text === "fake rule not set (A3)"))) fail("limits", "fake rule not set (A3)", answer.limits);
+    }
+  }
+  if (answer.map !== undefined) {
+    if (!isObject(answer.map)) fail("map", "ModuleMap", answer.map);
+    else {
+      array(answer.map.definitions, "map.definitions", node); array(answer.map.links, "map.links", link);
+      array(answer.map.entries, "map.entries", (entry, path) => {
+        if (!isObject(entry)) { fail(path, "entry", entry); return; }
+        node(entry.fn, path + ".fn"); array(entry.steps, path + ".steps", flowStep);
+      });
+      if (answer.map.siblings !== undefined) {
+        if (!isObject(answer.map.siblings)) fail("map.siblings", "siblings table", answer.map.siblings);
+        else {
+          array(answer.map.siblings.members, "map.siblings.members", (member, path) => {
+            if (typeof member !== "string") fail(path, "member file", member);
+          });
+          array(answer.map.siblings.rows, "map.siblings.rows", (row, path) => {
+            if (!isObject(row)) { fail(path, "sibling concern", row); return; }
+            if (typeof row.concern !== "string" || !row.concern || !["shared", "varies", "unclear"].includes(row.status as string)) fail(path, "named shared/varies/unclear concern", row);
+            array(row.cells, path + ".cells", (cell, at) => {
+              if (!isObject(cell) || typeof cell.member !== "string" || typeof cell.text !== "string" || !cell.text.trim()) fail(at, "member, text and at", cell);
+              else location(cell.at, at + ".at");
+            });
+          });
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  }
+  const collections = [answer.matches, answer.links];
+  if (isObject(answer.chain)) collections.push(answer.chain.up, answer.chain.down);
+  if (isObject(answer.tests)) collections.push(answer.tests.tests, answer.tests.undecided);
+  if (isObject(answer.map)) collections.push(answer.map.definitions, answer.map.links, answer.map.entries);
+  const empty = collections.every(value => value === undefined || (Array.isArray(value) && value.length === 0));
+  if (empty !== (answer.empty !== undefined)) fail("empty", empty ? "none found by static analysis" : "absent for a nonempty answer", answer.empty);
+  return failures;
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/matcher.ts b/code_map/eval/matcher.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c7fa853a59902a5c54d19be935b1de992f2134dd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/matcher.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+import { isDeepStrictEqual } from "node:util";
+
+export type LocationExpectation = { path: string; file: string; line: number };
+export type Expectation = {
+  includes: LocationExpectation[];
+  excludes: LocationExpectation[];
+  equals: { path: string; value: unknown }[];
+  ambiguous: boolean | null;
+  limitReasons: string[];
+};
+export type Mismatch = { path: string; expected: unknown; actual: unknown; message: string };
+
+export function isObject(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {
+  return value !== null && typeof value === "object" && !Array.isArray(value);
+}
+
+function descendants(value: unknown): unknown[] {
+  if (!isObject(value) || !Array.isArray(value.children)) return [];
+  return value.children.flatMap(child => [child, ...descendants(child)]);
+}
+
+/** Missing values stay absent; [] collects values, and children searches descendants. */
+export function selectPath(value: unknown, path: string): unknown[] {
+  let values: unknown[] = [value];
+  for (const segment of path.split(".")) {
+    const match = /^([A-Za-z_$][\w$]*)(\[\])?$/.exec(segment);
+    if (!match) throw new Error(`Invalid expectation path: ${path}`);
+    const key = match[1]!;
+    const array = Boolean(match[2]);
+    values = values.flatMap(parent => {
+      if (key === "children") return descendants(parent);
+      if (!isObject(parent) || !Object.hasOwn(parent, key)) return [];
+      const child = parent[key];
+      return array ? (Array.isArray(child) ? child : []) : [child];
+    });
+  }
+  return values;
+}
+
+export function collectLimitReasons(value: unknown): string[] {
+  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value.flatMap(collectLimitReasons);
+  if (!isObject(value)) return [];
+  const reasons: string[] = [];
+  if (Array.isArray(value.limits)) {
+    for (const limit of value.limits) {
+      if (isObject(limit) && typeof limit.reason === "string") reasons.push(limit.reason);
+    }
+  }
+  if (isObject(value.stop) && typeof value.stop.reason === "string") reasons.push(value.stop.reason);
+  for (const [key, child] of Object.entries(value)) {
+    if (key !== "limits" && key !== "stop") reasons.push(...collectLimitReasons(child));
+  }
+  return reasons;
+}
+
+export function matchAnswer(answer: unknown, expect: Expectation): Mismatch[] {
+  const failures: Mismatch[] = [];
+  for (const [rule, checks] of [["includes", expect.includes], ["excludes", expect.excludes]] as const) {
+    for (const check of checks) {
+      const actual = selectPath(answer, check.path);
+      const found = actual.some(value => isObject(value) && value.file === check.file && value.line === check.line);
+      if (found !== (rule === "includes")) failures.push({
+        path: check.path, expected: { [rule]: { file: check.file, line: check.line } },
+        actual, message: `${rule} location check failed`,
+      });
+    }
+  }
+  for (const check of expect.equals) {
+    const selected = selectPath(answer, check.path);
+    const actual = check.path.includes("[]") || check.path.split(".").includes("children") ? selected : selected[0];
+    if (!isDeepStrictEqual(actual, check.value)) failures.push({
+      path: check.path, expected: check.value, actual: actual === undefined ? { missing: true } : actual,
+      message: "equals check failed",
+    });
+  }
+  if (expect.ambiguous !== null) {
+    const actual = isObject(answer) ? answer.ambiguous : undefined;
+    if (actual !== expect.ambiguous) failures.push({ path: "ambiguous", expected: expect.ambiguous,
+      actual: actual ?? { missing: true }, message: "ambiguous check failed" });
+  }
+  const reasons = collectLimitReasons(answer);
+  for (const reason of expect.limitReasons) {
+    if (!reasons.includes(reason)) failures.push({ path: "limits/stop", expected: reason, actual: reasons,
+      message: "limit reason missing" });
+  }
+  return failures;
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/process.ts b/code_map/eval/process.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..32b058b2f2be1ec113969c7a57a3f9b9da6974c6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/process.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+import { createHash } from "node:crypto";
+import { lstat, readFile, readlink, readdir } from "node:fs/promises";
+import { join } from "node:path";
+
+export type ProcessResult = { exitCode: number; stdout: string; stderr: string; command: string[] };
+export type FileSnapshot = Record<string, string>;
+export type FileChange = { path: string; change: "added" | "removed" | "modified" };
+
+export function shellQuote(value: string): string { return "'" + value.replaceAll("'", "'\\''") + "'"; }
+
+export async function captureProcess(command: string[], cwd: string): Promise<ProcessResult> {
+  try {
+    const child = Bun.spawn(command, { cwd, stdout: "pipe", stderr: "pipe", stdin: "ignore" });
+    const [exitCode, stdout, stderr] = await Promise.all([child.exited, new Response(child.stdout).text(), new Response(child.stderr).text()]);
+    return { exitCode, stdout, stderr, command };
+  } catch (error) {
+    return { exitCode: -1, stdout: "", stderr: String(error), command };
+  }
+}
+
+export async function snapshotFiles(roots: string[]): Promise<FileSnapshot> {
+  const snapshot: FileSnapshot = {};
+  async function visit(path: string) {
+    if (Object.hasOwn(snapshot, path)) return;
+    const stat = await lstat(path, { bigint: true });
+    const metadata = `${stat.mode}:${stat.size}:${stat.mtimeNs}:${stat.ctimeNs}`;
+    if (stat.isSymbolicLink()) snapshot[path] = `symlink:${metadata}:${await readlink(path)}`;
+    else if (stat.isDirectory()) {
+      snapshot[path] = `directory:${stat.mode}:${stat.mtimeNs}:${stat.ctimeNs}`;
+      for (const entry of (await readdir(path)).sort()) await visit(join(path, entry));
+    } else if (stat.isFile()) snapshot[path] = `file:${metadata}:${createHash("sha256").update(await readFile(path)).digest("hex")}`;
+    else snapshot[path] = `other:${metadata}`;
+  }
+  for (const root of [...new Set(roots)].sort()) await visit(root);
+  return snapshot;
+}
+
+export function compareSnapshots(before: FileSnapshot, after: FileSnapshot): FileChange[] {
+  return [...new Set([...Object.keys(before), ...Object.keys(after)])].sort().flatMap(path => {
+    if (before[path] === after[path]) return [];
+    const change = before[path] === undefined ? "added" : after[path] === undefined ? "removed" : "modified";
+    return [{ path, change }];
+  });
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/report.ts b/code_map/eval/report.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..27adc7333d30648fc27a257e19366d8baead01c0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/report.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+import { requirementLines, uncheckedParts, type Requirement, type Status } from "./requirements.ts";
+import type { Mismatch } from "./matcher.ts";
+import type { ProcessResult, FileChange } from "./process.ts";
+
+export type CaseResult = {
+  id: string; source: string; requirement: Requirement; line: string; args: string[];
+  status: Status; reasons: string[]; failures: Mismatch[]; answer: unknown;
+  process: ProcessResult; isolation: boolean; changedFiles: FileChange[]; markerCreated?: boolean;
+};
+export type Observation = { id: string; requirement: Requirement; line: string; status: Status; reason?: string };
+
+export function aggregateStatus(statuses: Status[]): Status {
+  if (statuses.includes("NOT MET")) return "NOT MET";
+  if (!statuses.length || statuses.includes("NOT CHECKED")) return "NOT CHECKED";
+  return "MET";
+}
+
+function totals(statuses: Status[]) {
+  return Object.fromEntries((["MET", "NOT MET", "NOT CHECKED"] as const).map(status => [status, statuses.filter(item => item === status).length]));
+}
+
+export function buildReport(cases: CaseResult[], observations: Observation[], isolationProbe: ProcessResult) {
+  const requirements = Object.entries(requirementLines).map(([requirement, lines]) => {
+    const checks = lines.map(line => {
+      const casesForLine = cases.filter(result => result.requirement === requirement && result.line === line);
+      const observationsForLine = observations.filter(result => result.requirement === requirement && result.line === line);
+      const status = aggregateStatus([...casesForLine.map(result => result.status), ...observationsForLine.map(result => result.status)]);
+      const reasons = [...casesForLine.flatMap(result => result.reasons), ...observationsForLine.flatMap(result => result.reason ? [result.reason] : [])];
+      if (!casesForLine.length && !observationsForLine.length) reasons.push(requirement === "A6" ? "No opencode case files for the three modules were supplied." : requirement === "L2" ? "P5 measures cost against reading; this evaluator does not measure L2." : "No case exercises this Fails-if line.");
+      return { line, status, caseIds: casesForLine.map(result => result.id), observations: observationsForLine, reasons };
+    });
+    return { requirement, status: aggregateStatus(checks.map(check => check.status)), lines: checks };
+  });
+  return {
+    checker: "P2 Codex evaluator; authored independently of the future tool builder",
+    scope: "MET records the fixture/case checks assigned to this evaluator, not a proof for all repositories. Canned-stub results test the evaluator, not a real code-map tool.",
+    requirements, cases, uncheckedParts, isolationProbe,
+    totals: { requirements: totals(requirements.map(item => item.status)),
+      lines: totals(requirements.flatMap(item => item.lines.map(line => line.status))), cases: totals(cases.map(result => result.status)) },
+  };
+}
+
+export type Report = ReturnType<typeof buildReport>;
+
+export function renderReport(report: Report): string {
+  const rows = ["# Code-map evaluation", "", report.checker, "", report.scope, "", "| Requirement | Status |", "|---|---|"];
+  for (const requirement of report.requirements) rows.push(`| ${requirement.requirement} | ${requirement.status} |`);
+  rows.push("", "## Fails-if lines", "");
+  for (const requirement of report.requirements) {
+    for (const line of requirement.lines) {
+      rows.push(`- **${requirement.requirement} ${line.status}** — ${line.line}. Cases: ${line.caseIds.join(", ") || "none"}.`);
+      for (const reason of [...new Set(line.reasons)]) rows.push(`  - ${reason}`);
+    }
+  }
+  rows.push("", "## Failures", "");
+  for (const result of report.cases.filter(result => result.status === "NOT MET")) {
+    rows.push(`### ${result.id} (${result.requirement})`, "", `Case file: ${result.source}`, "", `Arguments: \`${JSON.stringify(result.args)}\``, "",
+      `Exit: ${result.process.exitCode}. Isolation: ${result.isolation}.`, "", "```json", JSON.stringify(result.failures, null, 2), "```", "",
+      "Tool stdout:", "```text", result.process.stdout, "```", "Tool stderr:", "```text", result.process.stderr, "```", "");
+  }
+  rows.push("## Parts not checked", "");
+  for (const part of report.uncheckedParts) rows.push(`- **${part.requirement} ${part.status}** — ${part.reason}`);
+  rows.push("", "## Totals", "", "```json", JSON.stringify(report.totals, null, 2), "```", "");
+  return rows.join("\n");
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/requirements.ts b/code_map/eval/requirements.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..631998d2ae0470e7e718fb6705d2a4f7a690ff5c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/requirements.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+export const requirementLines = {
+  R1: ["mapping a fixture whose top level writes a marker creates that marker"],
+  R2: [
+    "an implementation the lookup finds has no link",
+    "a declaration is presented as proof of an implementation",
+    "a test fake is unlabelled or presented as the real implementation",
+    "an unresolved or ambiguous target is unmarked",
+  ],
+  R3: ["protected content leaves the machine or enters git"],
+  A1: ["a claim lacks its location or contradicts the code, or a checked example misses a known item"],
+  A2: [
+    "a known place is not found",
+    "an ambiguous match is treated as certain, or a candidate not built is not named",
+    "a known link within the depth is missing, or a shown link contradicts the code",
+    "a link lacks its kind or location",
+    "a function reached twice is shown twice",
+  ],
+  A3: [
+    "the count differs from the list, or a link lacks its evidence",
+    "a test with a known path is missing",
+    "static links are called coverage",
+    "the per-function file report runs without the user's request",
+  ],
+  A5: ["an answer comes only inside a dump or without its evidence or limits, or a whole map is produced unasked"],
+  A6: ["fewer than three modules are mapped, or a map fails A1"],
+  L1: ["a branch stops early without a reason, or an empty result is presented as proof of absence"],
+  L2: ["it leaves out correctness, the build cost, the reading tokens or the time, or hides a worse result"],
+} as const;
+
+export type Requirement = keyof typeof requirementLines;
+export type Status = "MET" | "NOT MET" | "NOT CHECKED";
+
+export const uncheckedParts = [
+  { requirement: "A2", status: "NOT CHECKED", reason: "P6 checks the agent's selection and naming of candidates it did not build." },
+  { requirement: "A3", status: "NOT CHECKED", reason: "P6 checks whether the agent asks the user before requesting a per-function file report." },
+  { requirement: "A5", status: "NOT CHECKED", reason: "P6 checks whether the agent requests a whole map without being asked." },
+  { requirement: "R3", status: "NOT CHECKED", reason: "Network isolation and filesystem snapshots do not establish absence of caught connection attempts, transmission by other processes, or downstream training use." },
+] as const;
diff --git a/code_map/eval/run.ts b/code_map/eval/run.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5b1165f060188e0779a400c1d2e13175b2b02034
--- /dev/null
+++ b/code_map/eval/run.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@
+import { mkdir, rm, writeFile } from "node:fs/promises";
+import { resolve } from "node:path";
+import { loadCaseFile, type LoadedCaseFile, type EvalCase } from "./case-file.ts";
+import { validateAnswer } from "./contract.ts";
+import { matchAnswer, type Mismatch } from "./matcher.ts";
+import { captureProcess, compareSnapshots, shellQuote, snapshotFiles, type ProcessResult } from "./process.ts";
+import { buildReport, renderReport, type CaseResult, type Observation } from "./report.ts";
+import { requirementLines } from "./requirements.ts";
+
+export type EvalOptions = { tool: string; cases: string[]; out: string; cwd?: string };
+
+export function parseArguments(args: string[]): EvalOptions {
+  let tool = ""; let out = ""; const cases: string[] = [];
+  for (let index = 0; index < args.length; index++) {
+    const flag = args[index]; const value = args[++index];
+    if (!value || !["--tool", "--cases", "--out"].includes(flag!)) throw new Error("Usage: bun eval/run.ts --tool <command> [--cases <file>]... --out <dir>");
+    if (flag === "--tool") tool = value;
+    else if (flag === "--out") out = value;
+    else cases.push(value);
+  }
+  if (!tool.trim() || !out) throw new Error("--tool and --out are required");
+  if (!cases.length) cases.push(resolve(import.meta.dir, "cases/fixtures.json"));
+  return { tool, out: resolve(out), cases };
+}
+
+export function toolArguments(file: LoadedCaseFile, test: EvalCase): string[] {
+  return [...test.args, ...file.project.flatMap(project => ["--project", project]), "--root", file.root,
+    ...file.tests.flatMap(pattern => ["--tests", pattern]), "--json"];
+}
+
+async function evaluateCase(options: EvalOptions, file: LoadedCaseFile, test: EvalCase, probe: ProcessResult): Promise<CaseResult> {
+  const cwd = options.cwd ?? process.cwd();
+  const args = toolArguments(file, test);
+  const marker = file.root === resolve(import.meta.dir, "fixtures") ? resolve(file.root, "marker/EXECUTED.marker") : undefined;
+  if (marker) await rm(marker, { force: true });
+  const before = await snapshotFiles([file.root, cwd]);
+  const command = `${options.tool} ${args.map(shellQuote).join(" ")}`;
+  const isolation = probe.exitCode === 0;
+  const processResult = await captureProcess(isolation ? ["unshare", "-rn", "--", "sh", "-c", command] : ["sh", "-c", command], cwd);
+  const after = await snapshotFiles([file.root, cwd]);
+  const changedFiles = compareSnapshots(before, after);
+  const markerCreated = marker ? await Bun.file(marker).exists() : undefined;
+  if (marker) await rm(marker, { force: true });
+  const failures: Mismatch[] = [];
+  let answer: unknown = null;
+  if (processResult.exitCode !== 0) failures.push({ path: "$process.exitCode", expected: 0, actual: processResult.exitCode, message: processResult.stderr });
+  try {
+    answer = JSON.parse(processResult.stdout);
+    failures.push(...matchAnswer(answer, test.expect), ...validateAnswer(answer, test.args, file.tests));
+  } catch (error) {
+    failures.push({ path: "$stdout", expected: "one JSON Answer", actual: processResult.stdout, message: String(error) });
+  }
+  if (changedFiles.length) failures.push({ path: "$filesystem", expected: "no writes under root or working directory", actual: changedFiles, message: "R3 filesystem changed" });
+  if (markerCreated) failures.push({ path: "$marker", expected: "marker absent", actual: marker, message: "R1 repository source was executed" });
+  const reasons: string[] = [];
+  if (test.requirement === "R3" && !isolation) reasons.push(`unshare -rn unavailable (exit ${probe.exitCode}): ${probe.stderr.trim()}`);
+  if (test.requirement === "R1" && !marker) reasons.push("The case format has no marker path; only the bundled marker fixture has a runtime R1 check.");
+  const status = failures.length ? "NOT MET" : reasons.length ? "NOT CHECKED" : "MET";
+  return { id: test.id, source: file.source, requirement: test.requirement, line: test.line,
+    args, status, reasons, failures, answer, process: processResult, isolation, changedFiles, markerCreated };
+}
+
+export async function evaluate(options: EvalOptions) {
+  const files = await Promise.all(options.cases.map(loadCaseFile));
+  const probe = await captureProcess(["unshare", "-rn", "--", "true"], options.cwd ?? process.cwd());
+  const results: CaseResult[] = [];
+  const observations: Observation[] = [];
+  // Sequential runs make before/after snapshots attributable to one tool invocation.
+  for (const file of files) for (const test of file.cases) {
+    const result = await evaluateCase(options, file, test, probe);
+    results.push(result);
+    observations.push({ id: result.id, requirement: "R3", line: requirementLines.R3[0],
+      status: result.changedFiles.length ? "NOT MET" : probe.exitCode !== 0 ? "NOT CHECKED" : result.process.exitCode !== 0 ? "NOT MET" : "MET",
+      reason: probe.exitCode !== 0 ? `unshare -rn unavailable (exit ${probe.exitCode}): ${probe.stderr.trim()}` :
+        result.changedFiles.length ? "Tool changed files under root or working directory; see case evidence." :
+        result.process.exitCode !== 0 ? "Tool failed under network isolation; exit and output retained in case evidence." : undefined });
+  }
+  const moduleSuffixes = ["packages/core/src/session", "packages/core/src/tool", "packages/ai"];
+  const matchingA1Maps = results.filter(result => result.requirement === "A1" && result.args[0] === "map");
+  const moduleChecks = moduleSuffixes.map(suffix => matchingA1Maps.filter(result =>
+    result.args.some(arg => arg.replaceAll("\\", "/").replace(/\/$/, "").endsWith(suffix)) &&
+    (suffix !== "packages/core/src/tool" || result.args.some(arg => arg.replaceAll("\\", "/").endsWith("packages/core/src/permission.ts")))));
+  const allModulesChecked = moduleChecks.every(checks => checks.length > 0);
+  const allModulesMet = allModulesChecked && moduleChecks.every(checks => checks.every(check => check.status === "MET"));
+  for (const result of results.filter(result => result.requirement === "A6")) {
+    if (result.status === "NOT MET") continue;
+    if (!allModulesChecked) {
+      result.status = "NOT CHECKED";
+      result.reasons.push("A6 needs A1 map checks for all three opencode modules, including tool with permission.ts.");
+    } else if (!allModulesMet) {
+      result.status = "NOT MET";
+      result.failures.push({ path: "$A6", expected: "A1 passes for all three opencode module maps", actual: moduleChecks, message: "A module map failed A1" });
+    }
+  }
+  if (allModulesChecked) observations.push({ id: "A6-three-module-A1-checks", requirement: "A6", line: requirementLines.A6[0],
+    status: allModulesMet ? "MET" : "NOT MET", reason: "A6 is derived from A1 cases for the three specified opencode module-map commands." });
+  const report = buildReport(results, observations, probe);
+  await mkdir(options.out, { recursive: true });
+  await writeFile(resolve(options.out, "report.json"), JSON.stringify(report, null, 2) + "\n");
+  await writeFile(resolve(options.out, "report.md"), renderReport(report));
+  return report;
+}
+
+if (import.meta.main) {
+  try {
+    const options = parseArguments(Bun.argv.slice(2));
+    const report = await evaluate(options);
+    console.log("Requirements:", JSON.stringify(report.totals.requirements));
+    console.log("Fails-if lines:", JSON.stringify(report.totals.lines));
+    console.log("Cases:", JSON.stringify(report.totals.cases));
+    console.log("Report:", resolve(options.out, "report.json"));
+    if (report.cases.some(result => result.status === "NOT MET")) process.exitCode = 1;
+  } catch (error) {
+    console.error(String(error)); process.exitCode = 2;
+  }
+}
diff --git a/code_map/eval/stub/stub.ts b/code_map/eval/stub/stub.ts
